#!/usr/bin/env qore
# -*- mode: qore; indent-tabs-mode: nil -*-
# test-platform: macos - HTTP/1.x keep-alive reuse decided by the bytes buffered or readable on TCP and TLS sockets
# Copyright (C) 2026 Qore Technologies, s.r.o.

# An HTTP/1.x connection is not reused after a response when more data follows the response on it: whether the
# response has no body (a response to HEAD, 204, 304, or a Content-Length of 0) or a body that was read whole, the
# client closes the connection, and its next request is answered on a new connection (qore#7471); also when the data
# arrives in a write of its own after the response.  Nor is a connection reused after a 101 response to a request
# that asks for a protocol upgrade and does not take the connection over (a 101 response to a request that does not
# ask for one is an error, qore#7483), and a request after the server closed the connection (on a TLS connection,
# with its close_notify) is answered on a new connection.  A connection whose data ends with the response is still
# reused.  Both the HTTPClient class and the HttpClientIo connection manager are tested.

%modern

%prepend-module-path "${SCRIPT_DIR}/../../../../../qlib"
%requires QUnit
%requires HttpClientIo

%exec-class HttpClientResponseBoundaryReuseTest

#! a self-signed certificate for localhost, for the TLS server
